From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0031] meson-vdec: complete a drain on real completion, never
 certify a timeout, serialise the LAST decision

Incremental on top of 0030 (kernel #87). Answers the five concrete findings of
the 22.09 Codex review of 0030 against the effective #87 source:

1. drain_issued was set BEFORE codec_ops->drain(), so the EOS worker could
   hand out LAST while drain() was still delivering the DPB tail, and its
   200 ms quiet clock did not start from a completed drain. VP9/HEVC drain()
   (codec_vp9_flush_output / codec_hevc_flush_output) deliver the whole tail
   synchronously under their codec lock, so their return IS the completion:
   drain_done is now set after drain() returns and the worker is kicked at
   once - no quiet timer for these codecs. Their counter-based in-band LAST
   in dst_buf_done() is disabled, since it could cut drain()'s batch.
   The quiet timer remains only for codecs without .drain (H.264, MPEG-1/2),
   whose firmware has no "DPB empty" signal, and it now runs from the moment
   the EOS picture was actually queued (eos_queued_jiffies), not from STOP.
2. The 15 s branch skipped every gate and emitted a normal LAST. It now fires
   only if nothing has come out for 1 s, and the terminator carries
   V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR plus a dev_err naming what was missing.
3. No CAPTURE buffer for 60 ticks made the worker give up for good (the
   same infinite end-of-video hang). Now the terminator is marked pending
   and the next CAPTURE QBUF (vdec_vb2_buf_queue) re-arms the worker.
4. last_sent/sequence_cap were touched by the worker and the ISR-thread
   completion path with no common lock. The decision, sequence number and
   vb2 publication are now one transaction under a new eos_lock spinlock,
   in both paths; a real frame after LAST is counted and warned about.
   Lock facts from the source: DECODER_CMD runs under core->lock
   (vdev->lock), QBUF/STREAMOFF under sess->lock (m2m q_lock), so the two
   are NOT serialised with each other; the worker takes neither mutex
   (vdec_stop_streaming cancels it synchronously under sess->lock).
5. Generation guard: every STOP/START/stream on/off bumps eos_gen and a
   worker armed by an older STOP does nothing. The resume path of
   start_streaming now also cancels both works first. A repeated STOP while
   a drain is pending is a no-op instead of resetting state under the worker.

Terminator buffer ownership: taken from the m2m ready list. For VP9/HEVC,
after drain() the codec's frame lists are empty, so the firmware owns none of
those buffers. For H.264 the buffer was already recycled to the firmware as
free; the client re-queues the empty buffer before DEC_CMD_START, and
buf_output[idx] is cleared so that QBUF does not recycle the same index to the
firmware a second time.

---
diff -ruN base/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/esparser.c s1/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/esparser.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/esparser.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/esparser.c
@@ -405,9 +405,18 @@
 		if (codec_ops->eos_sequence) {
 			u32 len;
 			const u8 *data = codec_ops->eos_sequence(&len);
+			unsigned long flags;
 
-			sess->eos_queued = 1;
 			esparser_queue_eos(sess->core, data, len);
+			/*
+			 * h96 0031: otschet tishiny dlya terminatora h264 idet
+			 * ot momenta, kogda EOS-kartinka REALNO ushla v parser,
+			 * a ne ot STOP ili poslednego kadra.
+			 */
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&sess->eos_lock, flags);
+			sess->eos_queued = 1;
+			sess->eos_queued_jiffies = jiffies;
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&sess->eos_lock, flags);
 		}
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&sess->lock);
diff -ruN base/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c s1/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -264,8 +264,20 @@
 			sess->drain_total_ticks);
 		vdec_wait_inactive(sess);
 		if (codec_ops->drain) {
-			sess->drain_issued = 1;
+			unsigned long flags;
